<title>CROATIA: Croatian oil, natural gas output rises in August.</title>
<headline>Croatian oil, natural gas output rises in August.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Central Bureau of Statistics issued the following oil and natural gas output details.</p>
<p> CROATIA OIL EXTRACTION	AUGUST     JULY	 AUG '95</p>
<p> Crude oil (tonnes)	   122,972    117,746     127,509</p>
<p> Natural gas (000 cu m)     147,980    139,354     164,029</p>
<p>PETROLEUM PRODUCTS (tonnes)</p>
<p> Gasoline			 124,016    113,984     110,025</p>
<p> Gas oil			   68,833     73,204     107,437</p>
<p> Heating oil		    121,512    134,111     106,532</p>
<p>NOTE -- Data exludes production from Serb-held Eastern Slavonia, where outpout from some oilfields was restarted by state monopolist INA late in August.</p>
<p>-- Kolumbina Bencevic, Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
